# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Written for the longmotive-m.com cutover: the old ASP.NET CMS published the
# URLs below, and they are what Google has indexed. Every one of them 404s the
# moment Pages answers for the domain, so they are 301'd to the homepage.
#
# The new site is a single marketing page plus the .dc viewers -- the old
# about/services/projects/certifications pages are SECTIONS of that homepage,
# not separate documents, and the homepage exposes no id anchors to aim at.
# "/" is therefore the honest target for all of them.
#
# /data/* is deliberately absent: those are old CMS media files. A 404 is a
# truer answer for a missing image than a 301 to an HTML page.

/home                 /  301
/about-us             /  301
/services             /  301
/projects             /  301
/our-certifications   /  301

/gal/*                /  301
/cont/*               /  301
/usr/*                /  301

# The whole /prod/ tree was placeholder content -- category-01..03/021..023 and
# testing-product-1..12. Nothing there was ever real.
/prod/*               /  301

# The CMS served a parallel mobile site at /mobile/<same paths>.
/mobile/*             /  301
